<ProseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How MyRideSG collects, uses and protects your data — what the app records about you and your motorcycle, who it is shared with, and your choices over it."
  meta="Last updated: 1 September 2026"
>
  <h2>At a glance</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your bikes, logs and records belong to you. We never sell your data.</li>
    <li>
      Receipt and odometer scanning sends the photo to Google's Gemini API to read it.
      Fuel and odometer scans are read and discarded; service and expense receipts are
      kept with your log until you delete them.
    </li>
    <li>
      Location is used only while the app is open, to show workshops near you. We never
      track you in the background.
    </li>
    <li>
      Face ID / fingerprint unlock happens entirely on your device. Biometric data never
      reaches us.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can export everything, opt out of analytics, and delete your account — all
      in-app, no email required.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
  <p>
    MYRIDESG PTE. LTD. (UEN 202635558K) ("we", "us", or "our") operates the MyRideSG
    mobile application for iOS and Android and the website at <strong>myridesg.com</strong
    > (together, the "Service"). This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use,
    disclose, and safeguard your information when you use the Service. By using the
    Service, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this
    policy.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Account Information:</strong> You can sign in with Apple, with Google, or with
    a one-time email code. From Apple or Google we receive your name and email address
    (and profile picture, from Google) — never your password. If you choose Apple's
    <em>Hide My Email</em>, we only ever see the private relay address Apple creates for
    you.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Rider Data:</strong> Information you enter into the Service, including
    motorcycle details (make, model, plate number), maintenance logs, fuel fill-up
    records, mileage readings, expense records, and document expiry dates (COE,
    insurance, road tax).
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Photos You Scan:</strong> If you use the scan feature, the photo you take of a
    receipt, invoice, or odometer is processed as described in Section 4. Photos are only
    ever captured when you tap the scan or attach button — the app never reads your camera
    or photo library on its own.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Location:</strong> With your permission, your device location while the app is
    in use, so we can show workshops near you and how far away they are. See Section 7.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Usage and Device Data:</strong> Information about how the Service is used —
    screens opened, features used, device type and OS version. See Section 5.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Crash Reports:</strong> If the app crashes or something breaks, a technical
    report is sent to us. See Section 6.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide, operate, and maintain the Service</li>
    <li>To authenticate your identity and manage your account</li>
    <li>To store and display your motorcycle and maintenance data</li>
    <li>To read receipts and odometer photos you scan, so log forms can be filled in for you</li>
    <li>To send service reminders, expiry alerts, and push notifications you have opted into</li>
    <li>To calculate and display fuel efficiency, cost per km, and spending analytics</li>
    <li>To operate the XP rewards, quests, and loyalty programme</li>
    <li>To show workshops near you and let you contact or navigate to them</li>
    <li>To improve and personalise the Service</li>
    <li>To communicate important updates about the Service</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Receipt and Odometer Scanning</h2>
  <p>
    The scan feature uses AI to read the photo you take and fill in the log form for you.
    The photo is sent over an encrypted connection from our servers to Google's Gemini
    API, which returns the extracted fields (for example the workshop name, date, and
    amounts). Google processes these images solely to provide this service to us and does
    not use them to train its AI models.
  </p>
  <p>What happens to the photo depends on the type of scan:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Fuel and odometer scans</strong> are read and discarded — the photo is not
      stored anywhere after the fields are extracted.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Service invoices and expense receipts</strong> are kept with the log entry
      they belong to, so you can look at the original later. Deleting the log entry (or
      your account) deletes the photo.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Scanning is always optional — every form can be filled in by typing. Scans are
    rate-limited per rider per day to keep the feature fair and secure.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Usage Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We record how riders move through the app — which screens are opened, which features
    are used, and where a form is abandoned — so we can find what is confusing or broken
    and fix it. We rely on the Business Improvement exception under Singapore's Personal
    Data Protection Act for this.
  </p>
  <p>
    These records never contain your name, email address, phone number, vehicle plate
    number, NRIC, location, or anything you typed into the app. They are stored in our own
    database and are never sold or shared with advertisers or other companies. We keep
    this data for 180 days, after which it is deleted automatically. You can turn it off
    at any time under Account → Privacy and data → Share usage data, and deleting your
    account removes the link between these records and you.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Crash Reporting</h2>
  <p>
    We use Sentry, a crash-reporting service, to learn when the app crashes or an error
    occurs so we can fix it. Before a report leaves your device, we scrub it of personal
    details — vehicle plate numbers, email addresses, and phone numbers are removed.
    Reports contain technical context (device model, OS version, what the app was doing)
    rather than the content of your logs.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Location</h2>
  <p>
    If you grant location permission, we use your position <strong
      >only while the app is open</strong
    > to show nearby workshops and their distances. We do not track your location in the
    background, we do not keep a history of where you have been, and location is never
    attached to your fuel, service, or expense records. You can use the Service without
    granting location — workshop search simply won't sort by distance.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Biometric Unlock</h2>
  <p>
    You can choose to lock the app behind Face ID, Touch ID, or your device's fingerprint
    unlock. The biometric check is performed entirely by your device's operating system —
    your face or fingerprint data never leaves your device and is never visible to us.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Sign-In Providers</h2>
  <p>
    We use Apple and Google solely to authenticate you. We access only your basic profile
    information (name and email address) as permitted by the scopes you authorise — we do
    not access your iCloud, Gmail, Google Drive, contacts, or any other Apple or Google
    service data. Your use of these sign-in options is also governed by
    <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >Apple's Privacy Policy</a
    > and
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >Google's Privacy Policy</a
    >. One-time sign-in codes are delivered by our email provider, Postmark.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Service Providers</h2>
  <p>
    We share data with a small number of vendors, only so they can perform services for
    us, under their confidentiality and data-protection terms:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Supabase</strong> — cloud database, authentication, and file storage. This is
      where your account and rider data live.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Google Gemini API</strong> — reads the photos you scan (Section 4).</li>
    <li><strong>Google Maps</strong> — renders the workshop map inside the app.</li>
    <li><strong>Sentry</strong> — crash reporting (Section 6).</li>
    <li><strong>Postmark</strong> — delivers sign-in code and Service emails.</li>
    <li><strong>Expo</strong> — delivers push notifications and app updates.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We may also disclose data:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal Requirements:</strong> if required by law, regulation, or valid legal
      process.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Business Transfer:</strong> in the event of a merger, acquisition, or sale of
      assets, user data may be transferred with appropriate notice.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell, trade, or rent your personal information to anyone.</p>

  <h2>11. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
  <p>
    We retain your personal data for as long as your account is active. You can delete
    your account and associated data at any time, in-app, at Account → Privacy and data →
    Delete account — no need to contact support. Deletion is immediate and cannot be
    undone; some records may be retained where required by Singapore law. You can also
    export everything you have entered as a CSV backup from the same screen, and you may
    request deletion by contacting us at hello@myridesg.com if you prefer.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Data Security</h2>
  <p>
    We implement industry-standard security measures to protect your data, including
    encrypted connections (HTTPS/TLS), access controls, and secure cloud infrastructure.
    However, no method of transmission over the internet is 100% secure, and we cannot
    guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Your Rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
    <li>Request correction of inaccurate data</li>
    <li>Export your data (in-app, as CSV)</li>
    <li>Request deletion of your data</li>
    <li>Withdraw consent at any time by deleting your account</li>
    <li>Lodge a complaint with the Personal Data Protection Commission (PDPC) of Singapore</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To exercise any of these rights, contact us at hello@myridesg.com.</p>

  <h2>14. Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
  <p>
    On the website, we use browser local storage and session cookies to maintain your
    login session and application preferences (e.g., theme, settings). We do not use
    third-party advertising cookies. You may clear cookies and local storage through your
    browser settings, which will log you out of the Service.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The Service is not directed to individuals under the age of 16. We do not knowingly
    collect personal data from children under 16. If you believe we have inadvertently
    collected such data, please contact us immediately and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>16. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of significant
    changes by updating the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Continued use of
    the Service after changes constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
  </p>

  <h2>17. Governing Law</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy is governed by the laws of Singapore, including the Personal Data
    Protection Act 2012 (PDPA). Any disputes shall be subject to the exclusive
    jurisdiction of the courts of Singapore.
  </p>

